  "notes": "N=3 complete for all 8 tests (GT012-014, GT026-030), both arms, per docs/pack-ablation-protocol.md. GT013/014/026-030 round 1 (run 1) was manual Claude Code sessions; GT012 (all 3 runs) and GT013/014/026-030 rounds 2-3 were Agent-tool subagents (decided 2026-08-05, see PROGRESS.md), tagged method:'agent-tool-automated' on each such entry -- untagged entries are the manual runs. Result: kernel_only 100% (24/24), full_fef 100% (24/24) -- a complete tie, zero cap_reasons anywhere, no failure mode unique to either arm, across every run. Per the protocol's decision rule, a tie prefers kernel_only (smaller context cost). Caveat: Full FEF arm fidelity for the automated runs is not guaranteed identical to a real interactive Claude Code session (the fef.md prompt assumes 'the active runtime harness' autoloading via this repo's CLAUDE.md, which a subagent may or may not replicate exactly) -- this affects roughly 5/6 of the full_fef sample (20 of 24 runs). This result is on the 8 fixture-mode coding Golden Tests only and does not generalize to other routes (proposal, RCA, architecture review, etc.)."
